Correction follow-up for the Windows installed-brand / native-icon validation review.

Scope
- Branch: codex/windows-installed-brand-validation
- Review range: ec17340a..aa484039
- Windows-only release validation. Previously validated macOS work is outside this range.

Why this commit exists
The review confirmed the native icon implementation but found gaps around ICO frame guarantees, PowerShell source coverage, embedded C# compilation, reflection, Unicode/case-sensitive discovery, installed npm wrappers, and behavioral proof. The fixes use one source-policy entry point and bounded helpers rather than additional text searches.

Implemented guarantees
- ICO source frames are validated from decoded payload dimensions and native rendered content at 16, 32, 48, and 256 pixels.
- Native extraction is exercised in separate Windows PowerShell 5.1 and PowerShell 7 processes at both 16 and 32 pixels; dimensions and rendered hashes must agree.
- Repository PowerShell discovery uses unquoted Git paths and case-insensitive pathspecs, covering Unicode names and uppercase .PS1.
- Installed extension-host PowerShell wrappers are scanned through a bounded tree owner: 64 scripts, 20,000 entries, depth 32, internal junction deduplication, external traversal rejected.
- Add-Type compilation is closed to the three existing owners and exact source shapes. Embedded C# is inspected before compilation.
- Bounded static value flow covers variables, reassignment, concatenation, parentheses, Replace (case-insensitive), char/string casts, arrays, typed arrays, and PowerShell wildcards.
- Dynamic Add-Type access through variables, aliases, Get-Command/gcm, Invoke-Expression, ScriptBlock.Create, arrays, typed arrays, wildcards, and reordered parameters is rejected.
- Managed icon decoders through System.Drawing, WPF/XAML, reflection, GetType/GetMethod/GetConstructor families, and InvokeMember (including statically constructed member names) are rejected. The native owner's two exact GetMethod calls remain the only reflection exception.
- The generated npm/npx wrappers remain accepted; their dynamic execution does not compile managed code.
- The previous Node test was reduced from code-shape assertions to configuration and parsed-YAML contracts.
- Every modified or added code/test file is at or below 230 lines.

TDD evidence
Before implementation, dedicated fixtures failed for the reported forms: dynamic command/alias, ordinary embedded C#, URL/comment parsing, variable reflection, XAML, uppercase .PS1, Get-Command CommandInfo, Replace transformations, InvokeMember, wildcard/array inputs, System.Char casts, constructed member names, and typed arrays. The same fixtures pass after the implementation.

